<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="abs_fb_MachineFlow" Id="{25a90749-5412-41cc-ab55-c4e143997002}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*  abs_fb_MachineFlow - parallel machine-sequence composer (SFC-style token engine)
    on top of abs_fb_stateDevice.

    A derived FB declares its sequence as DATA in defineFlow() - addStep() for the
    steps, flow()/flowSplit2..3()/flowJoin2..3() (or addTransition() + arcFrom()/
    arcTo() for other shapes) for the relationships - and writes the step BODIES in
    stepActions(), a CASE over the step ids. The engine holds a token per active
    step: a transition fires when ALL its source steps are active AND done AND its
    permissive is TRUE; firing consumes the source tokens and activates all targets.
    Parallel branches, joins, choices (two transitions from one step with opposing
    permissives) and loops are therefore plain data - no flags, no duplicated states.

    Lifecycle (run/abort/retry/reset, interlocks, alarms, HMI commands) is inherited
    unchanged from abs_fb_stateDevice; the base state variable receives the
    transition-firing counter, so the base step timer measures time since the last
    firing (a stall watchdog). Per-step elapsed/timeout clocks run in the engine
    (parallel-safe); a step timeout faults with retry allowed - retry resumes with
    the timed-out step's clock cleared and all tokens in place.

    Usage:
        FUNCTION_BLOCK fb_SEQ_Wash EXTENDS abs_fb_MachineFlow
        Body (first line):       flowLogic();
        STEP IDS ARE `VAR CONSTANT`, NOT VAR. stepActions() dispatches on them with
        CASE, and IEC 61131-3 requires CASE labels to be CONSTANT - a runtime VAR
        holding addStep()'s return value cannot be a label and will not compile. So
        declare them as constants with explicit literal values, `c`-prefixed per
        CONVENTIONS §2 (never a type prefix - `cStepFill`, never `sFill`):

            VAR CONSTANT
                cStepFill : INT := 1;   // ids are assigned in addStep() CALL ORDER
                cStepHeat : INT := 2;
                cStepStir : INT := 3;
            END_VAR

        The constants and the addStep() order must agree, and nothing enforces it -
        inserting a step in the middle silently shifts every later id. addStep()
        returns the id it actually assigned, so guard it:

        Override defineFlow():   IF addStep('Fill tank', T#30S) <> cStepFill THEN
                                     setCfgError('flow: step id drift'); END_IF
                                 ...
                                 setInitialStep(cStepFill);
                                 flowSplit2(cStepFill, cStepHeat, cStepStir);
        Override stepActions():  CASE inpStepId OF cStepFill: ... stepDone(cStepFill); ...

        Transition ids are NOT dispatched on, so they may be plain VAR (`_transLoop`)
        holding what flow()/addTransition() returned - setPermissive() takes a value.
        A step completes via stepDone(id); a DONE step with no outgoing transition
        completes the sequence (setStateLogicDone). Override actionsAbort() for a
        controlled abort ramp (the default clears the tokens and finishes at once).

    Determinism: transitions are evaluated in ascending id order each scan; firing
    consumes tokens, so two transitions competing for one token resolve to the lower
    id. A newly activated step always executes at least one scan before any outgoing
    transition can fire.

    SELF-CONTAINED (CONVENTIONS §5): this FB references no GVL and holds no pointer
    to anything it does not own. A transition's gate is ONE BOOL - where the gate is
    really an fb_Permissive, the machine ANDs stsPermissiveOK in at the setPermissive()
    call, the same way it reports a step with stepDone(). The engine knows only tokens
    and booleans, which is all a token engine should know.

    Capacities are LITERALS, repeated in the array bounds and in every loop that walks
    them - keep those edits together:
      * 64 steps / 64 transitions. 64 is not arbitrary and is the one number NOT free
        to change: the HMI publishes the active/done/visited/fired/permissive masks as
        2 x UDINT (lo = 1..32, hi = 33..64), so raising it breaks that contract and the
        lhmi renderer with it. Widening means new mask members, not a bigger bound.
      * 4 sources / 4 targets per transition (ST_MachineFlow_Transition) - the widest
        AND-split or AND-join a transition can express.
      * 4095-byte stsFlowDef, the exported definition JSON. Truncation is reported, not
        silent (see actionsRun); step and transition NAMES are what consume it.

    HMI: HMIflow (ST_MachineFlow_HMI_Status) carries the token + permissive masks,
    the firing counter and the STATIC definition JSON including each transition's
    condition text (read once, on demand - ADS only, not for cyclic transport); the
    inherited HMIstateLogic carries state/commands. While the sequence runs,
    stsStepDescription is ENGINE-OWNED: the joined active-step names. Name every
    permissive-gated transition - the name is the operator's answer to 'why is this
    step stuck'. Step/transition names must not contain double quotes (def JSON).
*)
FUNCTION_BLOCK ABSTRACT abs_fb_MachineFlow EXTENDS abs_fb_stateDevice
VAR_OUTPUT
    stsActiveNames  : STRING(255);   // ' + '-joined names of the active steps
END_VAR
VAR
    HMIflow         : ST_MachineFlow_HMI_Status;
    _steps          : ARRAY[1..64] OF ST_MachineFlow_Step;
    _trans          : ARRAY[1..64] OF ST_MachineFlow_Transition;
    _stepTimers     : ARRAY[1..64] OF TON;
    _initialSteps   : ARRAY[1..64] OF BOOL;
    _stepCount      : INT;
    _transCount     : INT;
    _initialCount   : INT;
    _defined        : BOOL;
    _fireCount      : INT;    // the base state variable: transition firings this run
    _lastFired      : INT;
    _timeoutStep    : INT;    // step that raised the running step-timeout fault
    _wasRunning     : BOOL;
    _wasFaulted     : BOOL;
    _defLen         : INT;
    _defOverflow    : BOOL;
    _faultedStep    : INT;   // step that raised (or timed out into) the active fault; 0 = none
    _cfgError       : BOOL;
    _cfgErrorText   : STRING(255);
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Folder Name="flowBuilder" Id="{7ae9374c-9c3b-4520-8bff-64cbd42159ca}" />
    <Folder Name="flowRuntime" Id="{9d5c2015-1604-4168-a81c-fac4b8ebc62c}" />
    <Folder Name="Privates" Id="{414c5861-c8e1-4158-872e-8aa971a8e5e9}" />
    <Method Name="actionsAbort" Id="{ba4b5125-0d60-460c-9cae-fa8d8cd8e81b}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Default abort: drop all tokens and finish immediately. Override for a
// controlled ramp-down (make devices safe, then call setStateDoneAborting()).
METHOD PROTECTED actionsAbort : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[clearTokens();
setStateDoneAborting();
actionsAbort := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="actionsReset" Id="{99daa9d4-d9e3-4537-a38d-6c5150d03818}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PROTECTED actionsReset : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR
    t : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[clearTokens();
FOR t := 1 TO _transCount DO
    _trans[t].permissive := TRUE;
    _trans[t].fired := FALSE;
END_FOR
_fireCount := 0;
_lastFired := 0;
_timeoutStep := 0;
_faultedStep := 0;
actionsReset := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="actionsRun" Id="{3cbce039-b449-4145-a6db-b08b54461d5f}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The engine scan: per-step clocks/timeouts -> step bodies (once per active
// step) -> transition firing -> done detection. Runs every cycle while Running.
METHOD PROTECTED actionsRun : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF _cfgError THEN
    setStateLogicFault(_cfgErrorText, FALSE, 0);
    RETURN;
END_IF
IF _defOverflow THEN
    _defOverflow := FALSE;
    sendWarning('MachineFlow: definition JSON truncated - shorten step/transition names or widen stsFlowDef (4095)');
END_IF

runStepTimers();
IF stsFaulted THEN
    RETURN;   // a step timeout faulted this scan
END_IF
dispatchSteps();
fireTransitions();
checkFlowDone();
actionsRun := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="addStep" Id="{e7ac08b2-9c2b-4fd7-9814-995d0632e587}" FolderPath="flowBuilder\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Declare a step (call from defineFlow()). Returns the step id used by
// stepActions()/stepDone()/the transitions; 0 on capacity error.
// inpDescription = WHAT the step does, shown in the HMI's step popup.
METHOD PROTECTED addStep : INT
VAR_INPUT
    inpName        : STRING(63);
    inpTimeout     : TIME := T#0S;   // T#0S = no timeout; runtime override: setStepTimeout()
    inpDescription : STRING(125) := '';
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF _stepCount >= 64 THEN
    setCfgError('MachineFlow: addStep() capacity exceeded');
    addStep := 0;
    RETURN;
END_IF
_stepCount := _stepCount + 1;
_steps[_stepCount].name := inpName;
_steps[_stepCount].description := inpDescription;
_steps[_stepCount].timeout := inpTimeout;
addStep := _stepCount;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="addTransition" Id="{e1f46132-d311-4d37-b0fc-39c406e7354c}" FolderPath="flowBuilder\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Allocate an empty transition (call from defineFlow()); attach steps with
// arcFrom()/arcTo(). The flow*() helpers cover the common shapes.
// inpName is the CONDITION text the HMI shows on the transition bar
// (e.g. 'cycles < 3') - name every permissive so a held gate explains itself.
METHOD PROTECTED addTransition : INT
VAR_INPUT
    inpName : STRING(63) := '';
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF _transCount >= 64 THEN
    setCfgError('MachineFlow: addTransition() capacity exceeded');
    addTransition := 0;
    RETURN;
END_IF
_transCount := _transCount + 1;
_trans[_transCount].name := inpName;
addTransition := _transCount;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="appendDef" Id="{3a96c2d9-bfd5-4fae-82cc-ce76c7185434}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE appendDef : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpText : STRING(255);
END_VAR
VAR
    txtLen : INT;
    k      : INT;
    pSrc   : POINTER TO BYTE;
    pDst   : POINTER TO BYTE;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[txtLen := LEN(inpText);
IF txtLen = 0 THEN
    appendDef := TRUE;
    RETURN;
END_IF
IF _defLen + txtLen >= 4095 THEN
    _defOverflow := TRUE;
    RETURN;
END_IF
pSrc := ADR(inpText);
pDst := ADR(HMIflow.stsFlowDef);
pDst := pDst + _defLen;
FOR k := 0 TO txtLen - 1 DO
    pDst[k] := pSrc[k];
END_FOR
_defLen := _defLen + txtLen;
appendDef := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="arcFrom" Id="{f9720fde-5aa9-4bb5-b048-c3336b9e0a4d}" FolderPath="flowBuilder\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Add a SOURCE step to a transition (all sources must be done for it to fire).
METHOD PROTECTED arcFrom : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpTrans  : INT;
    inpStepId : INT;
END_VAR
VAR
    a : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF inpTrans < 1 OR inpTrans > _transCount OR inpStepId < 1 OR inpStepId > 64 THEN
    setCfgError('MachineFlow: arcFrom() bad transition/step id');
    RETURN;
END_IF
FOR a := 1 TO 4 DO
    IF _trans[inpTrans].sources[a] = 0 THEN
        _trans[inpTrans].sources[a] := inpStepId;
        arcFrom := TRUE;
        RETURN;
    END_IF
END_FOR
setCfgError('MachineFlow: arcFrom() arc capacity exceeded');
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="arcTo" Id="{e948893b-7c60-41bb-bc31-1fa4b89fc0c4}" FolderPath="flowBuilder\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Add a TARGET step to a transition (all targets activate when it fires).
METHOD PROTECTED arcTo : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpTrans  : INT;
    inpStepId : INT;
END_VAR
VAR
    a : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF inpTrans < 1 OR inpTrans > _transCount OR inpStepId < 1 OR inpStepId > 64 THEN
    setCfgError('MachineFlow: arcTo() bad transition/step id');
    RETURN;
END_IF
FOR a := 1 TO 4 DO
    IF _trans[inpTrans].targets[a] = 0 THEN
        _trans[inpTrans].targets[a] := inpStepId;
        arcTo := TRUE;
        RETURN;
    END_IF
END_FOR
setCfgError('MachineFlow: arcTo() arc capacity exceeded');
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="buildDefJson" Id="{737d46ea-7c35-4365-80ac-2ea338ba7e85}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE buildDefJson : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR
    i, t, a, sid : INT;
    firstArc   : BOOL;
    pEnd       : POINTER TO BYTE;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[_defLen := 0;
_defOverflow := FALSE;
appendDef('{"v":1,"steps":[');
FOR i := 1 TO _stepCount DO
    IF i > 1 THEN
        appendDef(',');
    END_IF
    appendDef('{"i":');
    appendDef(INT_TO_STRING(i));
    appendDef(',"n":"');
    appendDef(_steps[i].name);
    appendDef('"');
    IF _steps[i].description <> '' THEN
        appendDef(',"d":"');
        appendDef(_steps[i].description);
        appendDef('"');
    END_IF
    // Step TIMEOUT, in ms, and only when one is configured. Static config, so it belongs in the def
    // (read once) rather than in a cyclic member: 64 timeouts polled every scan would cost real
    // bandwidth for numbers that never change. Omitted when T#0S so an untimed step costs 0 bytes of
    // the 4095 - most steps have no timeout.
    IF _steps[i].timeout > T#0S THEN
        appendDef(',"to":');
        appendDef(UDINT_TO_STRING(TIME_TO_UDINT(_steps[i].timeout)));
    END_IF
    IF _initialSteps[i] THEN
        appendDef(',"init":1');
    END_IF
    appendDef('}');
END_FOR
appendDef('],"trans":[');
FOR t := 1 TO _transCount DO
    IF t > 1 THEN
        appendDef(',');
    END_IF
    appendDef('{"id":');
    appendDef(INT_TO_STRING(t));
    IF _trans[t].name <> '' THEN
        appendDef(',"n":"');
        appendDef(_trans[t].name);
        appendDef('"');
    END_IF
    appendDef(',"s":[');
    firstArc := TRUE;
    FOR a := 1 TO 4 DO
        sid := _trans[t].sources[a];
        IF sid > 0 THEN
            IF NOT firstArc THEN
                appendDef(',');
            END_IF
            appendDef(INT_TO_STRING(sid));
            firstArc := FALSE;
        END_IF
    END_FOR
    appendDef('],"t":[');
    firstArc := TRUE;
    FOR a := 1 TO 4 DO
        sid := _trans[t].targets[a];
        IF sid > 0 THEN
            IF NOT firstArc THEN
                appendDef(',');
            END_IF
            appendDef(INT_TO_STRING(sid));
            firstArc := FALSE;
        END_IF
    END_FOR
    appendDef(']}');
END_FOR
appendDef(']}');
pEnd := ADR(HMIflow.stsFlowDef);
pEnd := pEnd + _defLen;
pEnd^ := 0;
buildDefJson := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="checkFlowDone" Id="{57cb421d-d040-49c4-9112-011b669dbaea}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE checkFlowDone : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR
    i               : INT;
    anyActive       : BOOL;
    allTerminalDone : BOOL;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[allTerminalDone := TRUE;
FOR i := 1 TO _stepCount DO
    IF _steps[i].active THEN
        anyActive := TRUE;
        IF NOT _steps[i].done OR _steps[i].hasOutgoing THEN
            allTerminalDone := FALSE;
        END_IF
    END_IF
END_FOR
IF NOT anyActive THEN
    setStateLogicFault('MachineFlow: no active steps while running (check the flow definition)', FALSE, 0);
ELSIF allTerminalDone THEN
    setStateLogicDone();
END_IF
checkFlowDone := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="clearTokens" Id="{e71ff428-80d1-4afe-be09-b564253632b2}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Drop every token (and this run's history). PROTECTED because overriding actionsAbort() for a
// controlled ramp-down is a documented extension point, and the default it replaces ends with
// clearTokens() + setStateDoneAborting() - a subclass could not reproduce that while this was
// PRIVATE. Safe to expose: clearing mid-RUN is caught on the next scan by checkFlowDone, which
// faults with 'no active steps while running' rather than hanging silently, and during an abort
// actionsRun() is not running so the legitimate use never trips it.
METHOD PROTECTED clearTokens : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR
    i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[FOR i := 1 TO 64 DO
    _steps[i].active := FALSE;
    _steps[i].done := FALSE;
    _steps[i].visited := FALSE;
    _steps[i].entered := FALSE;
    _steps[i].kickTimer := TRUE;
END_FOR
clearTokens := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="defineFlow" Id="{cb032ed5-5433-46c1-abdf-c004ce83030c}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Override: declare the sequence graph - RELATIONSHIPS only, no step logic.
// addStep() the steps, then connect them with flow()/flowSplit2..3()/
// flowJoin2..3() (or addTransition() + arcFrom()/arcTo() for other shapes).
// Called once, before the first scan. Default initial step: the first declared
// one (override with setInitialStep(); call it more than once for parallel starts).
METHOD PROTECTED defineFlow : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="dispatchSteps" Id="{29885c72-cd4c-4726-8b50-f542033af305}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE dispatchSteps : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR
    i         : INT;
    firstScan : BOOL;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[FOR i := 1 TO _stepCount DO
    IF _steps[i].active THEN
        firstScan := NOT _steps[i].entered;
        _steps[i].entered := TRUE;
        stepActions(inpStepId := i, inpFirstScan := firstScan);
        // ATTRIBUTE A STEP-RAISED FAULT TO ITS STEP. A step body may check a condition and call
        // setFault() on the inherited state device: that faults the parent state machine, but the
        // fault also belongs to THIS step, and the HMI needs to know which one so the flow chart can
        // colour it red. Checked right after the body runs, and only claimed if nothing else has -
        // a step timeout (runStepTimers) already sets _faultedStep, and the first claim wins so a
        // later step in the same scan cannot steal the attribution.
        IF stsFaulted AND _faultedStep = 0 THEN
            _faultedStep := i;
        END_IF
    END_IF
END_FOR
dispatchSteps := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="finalizeFlow" Id="{8ad43b3c-1c37-4e39-9de8-cf191aadd296}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE finalizeFlow : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR
    t, a, sid : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// default initial step: the first declared one
IF _initialCount = 0 AND _stepCount > 0 THEN
    _initialSteps[1] := TRUE;
    _initialCount := 1;
END_IF
// derive hasOutgoing + validate every arc against the declared steps
FOR t := 1 TO _transCount DO
    FOR a := 1 TO 4 DO
        sid := _trans[t].sources[a];
        IF sid > 0 THEN
            IF sid > _stepCount THEN
                setCfgError('MachineFlow: a transition source references an unknown step');
            ELSE
                _steps[sid].hasOutgoing := TRUE;
            END_IF
        END_IF
        sid := _trans[t].targets[a];
        IF sid > _stepCount THEN
            setCfgError('MachineFlow: a transition target references an unknown step');
        END_IF
    END_FOR
END_FOR
buildDefJson();
HMIflow.stsStepCount := _stepCount;
HMIflow.stsTransCount := _transCount;
finalizeFlow := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="fireTransitions" Id="{7e0a5ae5-5dac-48c7-aaaf-8f3f099cc196}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE fireTransitions : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR
    t, a, sid   : INT;
    enabled   : BOOL;
    hasSource : BOOL;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[FOR t := 1 TO _transCount DO
    // A transition gate is ONE BOOL, and the engine knows nothing else about it. Where the gate is a
    // full fb_Permissive, the machine ANDs it in at the call site - setPermissive(t,
    // PermUnload.stsPermissiveOK) - exactly as it reports a step with stepDone(id). See the header:
    // this engine holds no reference to anything outside itself.
    enabled := _trans[t].permissive;
    hasSource := FALSE;
    FOR a := 1 TO 4 DO
        sid := _trans[t].sources[a];
        IF sid > 0 THEN
            hasSource := TRUE;
            IF NOT (_steps[sid].active AND _steps[sid].done) THEN
                enabled := FALSE;
            END_IF
        END_IF
    END_FOR
    IF enabled AND hasSource THEN
        // consume every source token first (a self-loop re-places below)
        FOR a := 1 TO 4 DO
            sid := _trans[t].sources[a];
            IF sid > 0 THEN
                _steps[sid].active := FALSE;
                _steps[sid].done := FALSE;
                // Consuming a token IS the moment a step completed. Recorded because the token is
                // gone next scan, leaving nothing to distinguish "finished" from "never ran" - which
                // the flow chart colours differently.
                _steps[sid].visited := TRUE;
            END_IF
        END_FOR
        FOR a := 1 TO 4 DO
            sid := _trans[t].targets[a];
            IF sid > 0 THEN
                placeToken(sid);
            END_IF
        END_FOR
        _lastFired := t;
        _trans[t].fired := TRUE;   // this run; _lastFired only ever holds the newest
        _fireCount := _fireCount + 1;
    END_IF
END_FOR
fireTransitions := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="flow" Id="{9eae2287-a065-4375-b9a7-11aa1f5effb1}" FolderPath="flowBuilder\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Simple arrow: source done -> target activates. Returns the transition id
// (keep it to attach a runtime permissive via setPermissive(), e.g. for loop-back edges).
// inpName = the condition text shown on the HMI bar.
METHOD PROTECTED flow : INT
VAR_INPUT
    inpFrom : INT;
    inpTo   : INT;
    inpName : STRING(63) := '';
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[flow := addTransition(inpName := inpName);
IF flow = 0 THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF
arcFrom(inpTrans := flow, inpStepId := inpFrom);
arcTo(inpTrans := flow, inpStepId := inpTo);
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="flowJoin2" Id="{b966260c-5420-49d1-8a80-00e48764cb29}" FolderPath="flowBuilder\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// AND-convergence: fires when BOTH sources are done; activates the target.
METHOD PROTECTED flowJoin2 : INT
VAR_INPUT
    inpFrom1 : INT;
    inpFrom2 : INT;
    inpTo    : INT;
    inpName  : STRING(63) := '';
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[flowJoin2 := addTransition(inpName := inpName);
IF flowJoin2 = 0 THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF
arcFrom(inpTrans := flowJoin2, inpStepId := inpFrom1);
arcFrom(inpTrans := flowJoin2, inpStepId := inpFrom2);
arcTo(inpTrans := flowJoin2, inpStepId := inpTo);
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="flowJoin3" Id="{52896894-2b9f-4f4b-a419-680f01545d1e}" FolderPath="flowBuilder\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// AND-convergence: fires when ALL THREE sources are done; activates the target.
METHOD PROTECTED flowJoin3 : INT
VAR_INPUT
    inpFrom1 : INT;
    inpFrom2 : INT;
    inpFrom3 : INT;
    inpTo    : INT;
    inpName  : STRING(63) := '';
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[flowJoin3 := addTransition(inpName := inpName);
IF flowJoin3 = 0 THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF
arcFrom(inpTrans := flowJoin3, inpStepId := inpFrom1);
arcFrom(inpTrans := flowJoin3, inpStepId := inpFrom2);
arcFrom(inpTrans := flowJoin3, inpStepId := inpFrom3);
arcTo(inpTrans := flowJoin3, inpStepId := inpTo);
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="flowLogic" Id="{b84fd3d9-1365-43f6-9a41-32e8e9e50fae}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Call as the FIRST line of the derived FB's body (like DeviceLogic() in
// abs_fb_Device). Builds the graph once, handles run/resume edges, then runs
// the inherited state logic (which calls actionsRun = the engine scan).
METHOD PROTECTED flowLogic : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF NOT _defined THEN
    _defined := TRUE;
    defineFlow();
    finalizeFlow();
END_IF

// Run/resume edge: a fresh run seeds the initial tokens; a retry-resume keeps
// the tokens in place and only restarts the timed-out step's clock.
IF stsRunning AND NOT _wasRunning THEN
    IF _wasFaulted THEN
        IF _timeoutStep > 0 THEN
            _steps[_timeoutStep].kickTimer := TRUE;
            _timeoutStep := 0;
_faultedStep := 0;
        END_IF
    ELSE
        seedTokens();
    END_IF
END_IF
_wasRunning := stsRunning;
_wasFaulted := stsFaulted;

stateLogic(ADR(_fireCount));
publishHMI();
flowLogic := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="flowSplit2" Id="{f7b4bf83-634f-43b3-abf4-99d3bdf235a1}" FolderPath="flowBuilder\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// AND-divergence: source done -> BOTH targets activate (parallel branches).
METHOD PROTECTED flowSplit2 : INT
VAR_INPUT
    inpFrom : INT;
    inpTo1  : INT;
    inpTo2  : INT;
    inpName : STRING(63) := '';
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[flowSplit2 := flow(inpFrom := inpFrom, inpTo := inpTo1, inpName := inpName);
IF flowSplit2 = 0 THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF
arcTo(inpTrans := flowSplit2, inpStepId := inpTo2);
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="flowSplit3" Id="{8b910b48-f04f-48a5-b97c-bfba88a6f918}" FolderPath="flowBuilder\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// AND-divergence: source done -> ALL THREE targets activate (parallel branches).
METHOD PROTECTED flowSplit3 : INT
VAR_INPUT
    inpFrom : INT;
    inpTo1  : INT;
    inpTo2  : INT;
    inpTo3  : INT;
    inpName : STRING(63) := '';
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[flowSplit3 := flow(inpFrom := inpFrom, inpTo := inpTo1, inpName := inpName);
IF flowSplit3 = 0 THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF
arcTo(inpTrans := flowSplit3, inpStepId := inpTo2);
arcTo(inpTrans := flowSplit3, inpStepId := inpTo3);
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="getFlowHMIdata" Id="{54890c2c-d0bc-4142-8837-18c665828b26}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PUBLIC getFlowHMIdata : ST_MachineFlow_HMI_Status
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[getFlowHMIdata := HMIflow;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="placeToken" Id="{e4889f10-40aa-4317-91ec-55c7088989bb}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE placeToken : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpStepId : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[_steps[inpStepId].active := TRUE;
_steps[inpStepId].done := FALSE;
_steps[inpStepId].entered := FALSE;
_steps[inpStepId].kickTimer := TRUE;   // restart the elapsed clock (also on re-entry)
placeToken := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="publishHMI" Id="{35ccff2f-cf60-4cf6-873b-1e92a6f10c06}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE publishHMI : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR
    i     : INT;
    t     : INT;
    lo    : UDINT;
    hi    : UDINT;
    dLo   : UDINT;
    dHi   : UDINT;
    pLo   : UDINT;
    pHi   : UDINT;
    vLo   : UDINT;
    vHi   : UDINT;
    fLo   : UDINT;
    fHi   : UDINT;
    names : STRING(255);
    n     : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[FOR i := 1 TO _stepCount DO
    IF _steps[i].active THEN
        IF i <= 32 THEN
            lo := lo OR SHL(TO_UDINT(1), i - 1);
            IF _steps[i].done THEN
                dLo := dLo OR SHL(TO_UDINT(1), i - 1);
            END_IF
        ELSE
            hi := hi OR SHL(TO_UDINT(1), i - 33);
            IF _steps[i].done THEN
                dHi := dHi OR SHL(TO_UDINT(1), i - 33);
            END_IF
        END_IF
        IF n > 0 THEN
            names := CONCAT(names, ' + ');
        END_IF
        names := CONCAT(names, _steps[i].name);
        n := n + 1;
    END_IF
    // Outside the .active guard on purpose: a COMPLETED step has no token, so this bit is exactly
    // the information the active mask cannot carry.
    IF _steps[i].visited THEN
        IF i <= 32 THEN
            vLo := vLo OR SHL(TO_UDINT(1), i - 1);
        ELSE
            vHi := vHi OR SHL(TO_UDINT(1), i - 33);
        END_IF
    END_IF
END_FOR
FOR t := 1 TO _transCount DO
    // This mask IS the effective gate, because the boolean is: whatever ANDs into a transition's
    // permissive - a plain condition, an fb_Permissive's stsPermissiveOK, both - the machine ANDs in
    // before calling setPermissive(). Reporting a ready gate on a sequence that cannot advance would
    // be the exact symptom an operator is using the flow chart to diagnose.
    IF _trans[t].permissive THEN
        IF t <= 32 THEN
            pLo := pLo OR SHL(TO_UDINT(1), t - 1);
        ELSE
            pHi := pHi OR SHL(TO_UDINT(1), t - 33);
        END_IF
    END_IF
    IF _trans[t].fired THEN
        IF t <= 32 THEN
            fLo := fLo OR SHL(TO_UDINT(1), t - 1);
        ELSE
            fHi := fHi OR SHL(TO_UDINT(1), t - 33);
        END_IF
    END_IF
END_FOR
HMIflow.stsActiveLo := lo;
HMIflow.stsActiveHi := hi;
HMIflow.stsDoneLo := dLo;
HMIflow.stsDoneHi := dHi;
HMIflow.stsPermissiveLo := pLo;
HMIflow.stsPermissiveHi := pHi;
HMIflow.stsVisitedLo := vLo;
HMIflow.stsVisitedHi := vHi;
HMIflow.stsFiredLo := fLo;
HMIflow.stsFiredHi := fHi;
HMIflow.stsFaultedStep := _faultedStep;
HMIflow.stsFireCount := _fireCount;
HMIflow.stsLastFired := _lastFired;
stsActiveNames := names;
HMIflow.stsActiveNames := names;   // was declared but never written - see Docs/fb_MachineFlow_Design.md
IF stsRunning AND n > 0 THEN
    stsStepDescription := names;   // engine-owned while running
END_IF
publishHMI := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="runStepTimers" Id="{8408a303-0cc8-40ca-9c4d-49f50547d1be}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE runStepTimers : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR
    i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[FOR i := 1 TO _stepCount DO
    // kickTimer forces one scan of IN=FALSE so the TON restarts on token placement
    _stepTimers[i](IN := _steps[i].active AND NOT _steps[i].kickTimer, PT := T#100H);
    IF _steps[i].kickTimer THEN
        _steps[i].kickTimer := FALSE;
    ELSIF _steps[i].active AND _steps[i].timeout > T#0S AND _stepTimers[i].ET > _steps[i].timeout THEN
        _timeoutStep := i;
        _faultedStep := i;   // a timeout is a step fault too — same red step on the chart
        setStateLogicFault(CONCAT('Step timeout: ', _steps[i].name), TRUE, _fireCount);
        RETURN;
    END_IF
END_FOR
runStepTimers := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="seedTokens" Id="{e13412f3-8b3e-455d-b56f-26180532d1dd}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE seedTokens : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR
    i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[clearTokens();
_fireCount := 0;
_lastFired := 0;
_timeoutStep := 0;
_faultedStep := 0;
FOR i := 1 TO _stepCount DO
    IF _initialSteps[i] THEN
        placeToken(i);
    END_IF
END_FOR
seedTokens := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="setCfgError" Id="{3531508c-8055-44c5-aa40-6f1dc5ea0cd8}" FolderPath="Privates\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Latch the FIRST definition error; actionsRun() faults on any run attempt.
// Report a CONFIGURATION error - a defineFlow() mistake, not a runtime fault. actionsRun turns it
// into a non-retryable fault, because a bad graph cannot be retried into a good one. PROTECTED so a
// subclass's defineFlow() can report its own (e.g. the addStep() id-drift guard in the header).
METHOD PROTECTED setCfgError : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpMessage : STRING(255);
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF NOT _cfgError THEN
    _cfgError := TRUE;
    _cfgErrorText := inpMessage;
END_IF
setCfgError := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="setPermissive" Id="{cb1660d2-9b0f-49ce-96ff-78a6502e59fb}" FolderPath="flowRuntime\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Set a transition's permissive - the condition that must be MET to proceed
// (call from stepActions(), typically in the SOURCE step's body). Permissives
// are sticky and reset to TRUE on reset. OR-choice: opposing permissives on
// two transitions leaving the same step.
METHOD PROTECTED setPermissive : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpTrans     : INT;
    inpCondition : BOOL;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF inpTrans >= 1 AND inpTrans <= _transCount THEN
    _trans[inpTrans].permissive := inpCondition;
    setPermissive := TRUE;
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="setInitialStep" Id="{286b86d1-09fa-4da9-aa79-d74fe87d5812}" FolderPath="flowBuilder\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Mark a step as initially active on run (call from defineFlow(), AFTER the
// steps are declared; more than once for parallel starts). Default: step 1.
METHOD PROTECTED setInitialStep : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpStepId : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF inpStepId < 1 OR inpStepId > _stepCount THEN
    setCfgError('MachineFlow: setInitialStep() unknown step');
    RETURN;
END_IF
IF NOT _initialSteps[inpStepId] THEN
    _initialSteps[inpStepId] := TRUE;
    _initialCount := _initialCount + 1;
END_IF
setInitialStep := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="setStepTimeout" Id="{4e0691a4-9f69-4f57-ad04-d9d2fb8205ec}" FolderPath="flowRuntime\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Runtime timeout override (e.g. from a recipe) - replaces the addStep() value.
METHOD PROTECTED setStepTimeout : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpStepId  : INT;
    inpTimeout : TIME;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF inpStepId >= 1 AND inpStepId <= _stepCount THEN
    _steps[inpStepId].timeout := inpTimeout;
    setStepTimeout := TRUE;
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="stepActions" Id="{c59d1cb4-51fa-446e-bd5e-56d9801c1363}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Override: the step BODIES - a CASE over the ids returned by addStep().
// Called once per ACTIVE step per scan (parallel steps each get their call);
// inpFirstScan is TRUE the first scan after the step's token arrives (use it
// for one-shot commands). Report completion with stepDone(inpStepId); fault
// via the inherited setStateLogicFault().
METHOD PROTECTED stepActions : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpStepId    : INT;
    inpFirstScan : BOOL;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="stepActive" Id="{568b84bb-e9ad-4523-af5e-086387da9ce1}" FolderPath="flowRuntime\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PROTECTED stepActive : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpStepId : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF inpStepId >= 1 AND inpStepId <= _stepCount THEN
    stepActive := _steps[inpStepId].active;
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="stepDone" Id="{d31c5ef4-359a-42c7-aa06-c84100ab9f6b}" FolderPath="flowRuntime\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Report a step complete (call from stepActions()). The token stays in place,
// marked done, until an outgoing transition consumes it - or, if the step has
// no outgoing transition, the sequence completes.
METHOD PROTECTED stepDone : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    inpStepId : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF inpStepId >= 1 AND inpStepId <= _stepCount THEN
    IF _steps[inpStepId].active THEN
        _steps[inpStepId].done := TRUE;
        stepDone := TRUE;
    END_IF
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="stepElapsed" Id="{763d77fc-0313-463c-987a-eea37dc346af}" FolderPath="flowRuntime\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Time since this step's token arrived (each step has its own clock).
METHOD PROTECTED stepElapsed : TIME
VAR_INPUT
    inpStepId : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF inpStepId >= 1 AND inpStepId <= _stepCount THEN
    stepElapsed := _stepTimers[inpStepId].ET;
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>
